# ============================================================
# BLUEGRID LAND SOLUTIONS
#
# This is a no-build static site, so there are no dependency or
# artifact directories to exclude. Everything below is deliberate.
# ============================================================

# ── Marketing collateral ──
#
# Graphics produced for marketing rather than for the website —
# Google Business Profile service tiles, post images, cover art.
# Nothing in index.html, the service pages, the location pages, or
# the stylesheets references them, and they are large exports that
# would bloat the repository for no benefit.
#
# Kept locally so the owner has them to hand; not uploaded.
#
# This replaced "graphics/GBP - Services/" on 2026-08-20, when the
# exports moved to graphics/marketingAssets/GBP/. The rule covers the
# whole marketingAssets tree rather than one GBP folder, so the next
# batch of collateral is ignored without anyone remembering to add a
# rule. That matters: these arrived briefly at the repository root,
# where nothing ignored them and a broad "git add -A" would have
# committed 9MB of them.

graphics/marketingAssets/

# ── The owner video's archival master ──
#
# graphics/videos/IntroVideoFromChase.mp4 is Chase's original recording,
# 9MB, and nothing on the site loads it. What the site serves is
# chaseIntro.web.mp4 beside it — a lossless `-c copy -movflags
# +faststart` remux whose video and audio bitstreams hash identically to
# the master's. The master is the source; the web copy is the artifact.
#
# It is excluded for the same reason as the marketing collateral above,
# and one more besides: this repository is published with GitHub Pages,
# so committing it would put a 9MB file into Git history permanently AND
# make it publicly downloadable, to serve a file no page references.
# Deleting it in a later commit would not shrink the history.
#
# Archived at ClientSites/_archive/client_BluegridLandSolutions/video/,
# outside this repository, before this rule was added. A copy is kept
# here too so it is to hand — same arrangement as the collateral above.
#
# THE THREE FILES BESIDE IT ARE PRODUCTION ASSETS AND MUST STAY TRACKED:
# chaseIntro.web.mp4, chaseIntro.poster.webp and chaseIntro.en.vtt are
# all referenced from js/indexJS.js. Do not widen this into a
# graphics/videos/ rule or the owner introduction section breaks.

graphics/videos/IntroVideoFromChase.mp4

# ── QA tooling dependencies ──
#
# _qa/ holds the browser validation suite and is tracked. Its one npm
# dependency is not.

_qa/node_modules/

# ── Local session-closeout SOP ──
#
# A workflow instruction file for Claude sessions, not project content.
# Stays local; never tracked, never committed.

docs/sessionCloseout.md

graphics/logos/TPname.png
graphics/logos/masterFavicon_BG.png
